    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0293" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg233"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to
                        Messrs. Goodrich, Beady &amp;
                    Goodrich</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Your letter of the 26th ultimo, and
                    the affidavit of Mr. A. F. Stubbs, have been examined in connection with the
                    papers already on file here relative to the schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Henry Crosby</hi>, and in reply I have to say that I see no reason to
                    change the opinion expressed in the Department’s letter to you under date of
                    April 10 last.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
